  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">South Sudan START HUB cordination</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Hub Members have agreed to form a consortium of humanitarian civil society organizations called South Sudan Hub, currently under incubation within the Start Network, with the collective commitment to enable a localised; community centric hub responding to needs defined by the affected community in South Sudan. Through a host selection process, the Hub has agreed that CAFOD should be the Host Agency in relation to the Hub, from 1 October 2024 to December 2025 as agreed with the Hub Members.
The role of the Host Agency is to provide the operational and administrative functions necessary to deliver the activities and/or programmes it is hosting on behalf of the Hub. The host agency will apply its own administrative procedures in hub operations and functions, as applicable, in accordance with any Hub Leadership Team guidelines and as required by specific grant agreements.</narrative>
  </description>
